IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `eia-core`
IMPORT `eia-core-interpretation`
IMPORT `ei3-part4-deduction`

-- Tests of ei3-part4-deduction.l4 (Act ss 81 to 84).
-- Expected values are hand-worked from the text of the section named beside each assertion. Every figure is invented.

§ `s 81 interpretation`

#ASSERT `s 81 authorized person` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 81 authorized person` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 81 judge` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 81 judge` FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 81 judge` FALSE FALSE)
-- "Minister" in Part IV is the Minister of National Revenue (the keel answers it).
#ASSERT `s 2(1) the Minister for` `Part IV` EQUALS `the Minister of National Revenue`

§ `s 82(1)(a) and (2) deducting, and the maximum`

-- Earnings paid by this employer so far, against a maximum of 39,000: 38,999.99 has not reached it; 39,000 has; more has.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(2) the employer shall not make any deduction for the year` 38_999.99 39_000)
#ASSERT `s 82(2) the employer shall not make any deduction for the year` 39_000 39_000
#ASSERT `s 82(2) the employer shall not make any deduction for the year` 45_000 39_000
#ASSERT `s 82(1)(a) the employer must deduct the prescribed amount from the remuneration` TRUE 10_000 39_000
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(1)(a) the employer must deduct the prescribed amount from the remuneration` TRUE 39_000 39_000)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(1)(a) the employer must deduct the prescribed amount from the remuneration` FALSE 10_000 39_000)

§ `s 82(1)(b) remitting`

-- Deducted 50 and employer's premium 70: at least 120 to the Receiver General by the prescribed day (15 February 2027), in the prescribed manner.
#ASSERT `s 82(1)(b) the employer has remitted as the paragraph requires` 50 70 120 (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15) TRUE
#ASSERT `s 82(1)(b) the employer has remitted as the paragraph requires` 50 70 130 (YearMonthDay 2027 2 10) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15) TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(1)(b) the employer has remitted as the paragraph requires` 50 70 119.99 (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(1)(b) the employer has remitted as the paragraph requires` 50 70 120 (YearMonthDay 2027 2 16) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(1)(b) the employer has remitted as the paragraph requires` 50 70 120 (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15) FALSE)

§ `s 82(3) and (3.1) remitting at a financial institution`

#ASSERT `s 82(3) the remittance was made as the subsection requires` FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 82(3) the remittance was made as the subsection requires` TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(3) the remittance was made as the subsection requires` TRUE FALSE)
-- Remitted to the Receiver General at least one day before the due day (15 February): on the 14th yes, on the 15th no.
#ASSERT `s 82(3.1) the prescribed person is deemed to have remitted the amount to the account at a financial institution` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 2 14) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(3.1) the prescribed person is deemed to have remitted the amount to the account at a financial institution` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15))
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(3.1) the prescribed person is deemed to have remitted the amount to the account at a financial institution` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2027 2 1) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15))

§ `s 82(4) to (7) failure to deduct`

-- (5): (a) a ruling that no deduction is needed, (b) not based on incorrect material information, (c) later decided otherwise.
#ASSERT `s 82(5) the employer is not liable for failing to make the deduction` TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(5) the employer is not liable for failing to make the deduction` TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(5) the employer is not liable for failing to make the deduction` FALSE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(5) the employer is not liable for failing to make the deduction` TRUE FALSE FALSE)
-- Once the decision is communicated, liable (without interest or penalties) for the employer's premium.
#ASSERT `s 82(5) the employer is liable, without interest or penalties, to pay the employer's premium` TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(5) the employer is liable, without interest or penalties, to pay the employer's premium` TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(5) the employer is liable, without interest or penalties, to pay the employer's premium` TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
-- (4): liable for the whole amount, subject to (5).
#ASSERT `s 82(4) the employer is liable to pay Her Majesty the whole amount` TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(4) the employer is liable to pay Her Majesty the whole amount` TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(4) the employer is liable to pay Her Majesty the whole amount` FALSE FALSE)
-- (6): a payment made on 10 March 2026; a subsequent payment within 12 months (to 10 March 2027), with at most one other missed premium.
#ASSERT `s 82(6) the employer may deduct the premium it failed to deduct from the subsequent payment` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 10) 1
#ASSERT `s 82(6) the employer may deduct the premium it failed to deduct from the subsequent payment` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 17) 0
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(6) the employer may deduct the premium it failed to deduct from the subsequent payment` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2027 3 11) 1)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(6) the employer may deduct the premium it failed to deduct from the subsequent payment` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 6 1) 2)
-- A "subsequent" payment is after the first one.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(6) the employer may deduct the premium it failed to deduct from the subsequent payment` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) 0)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(6) the employer may deduct the premium it failed to deduct from the subsequent payment` (YearMonthDay 2026 3 10) (YearMonthDay 2026 3 9) 0)
-- 12 months after 29 February 2024 clamps to 28 February 2025.
#ASSERT `s 82(6) the employer may deduct the premium it failed to deduct from the subsequent payment` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2025 2 28) 0
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(6) the employer may deduct the premium it failed to deduct from the subsequent payment` (YearMonthDay 2024 2 29) (YearMonthDay 2025 3 1) 0)
-- (7): deemed received at that time.
#ASSERT `s 82(7) the day on which the insured person is deemed to have received the amount` TRUE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 15) EQUALS JUST (YearMonthDay 2026 5 15)
#ASSERT `s 82(7) the day on which the insured person is deemed to have received the amount` FALSE (YearMonthDay 2026 5 15) EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 82(8) and (9) interest and penalty`

#ASSERT `s 82(8) the employer shall pay interest to the Receiver General` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(8) the employer shall pay interest to the Receiver General` FALSE)
-- Due 15 February 2027, remitted 25 February 2027: interest runs over that period, both days counted (11 days).
#ASSERT `s 82(8) the period for which interest is computed` (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 25) EQUALS `Period of days` OF (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15), (YearMonthDay 2027 2 25)
#ASSERT `the number of days in` (`s 82(8) the period for which interest is computed` (YearMonthDay 2027 2 15) (YearMonthDay 2027 2 25)) EQUALS 11
-- (9) failure: received on time and in the required manner is no failure; late, or not in the manner, or never, is.
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(9) there was a failure to remit` (JUST 0) TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82(9) there was a failure to remit` (JUST (0 MINUS 2)) TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 82(9) there was a failure to remit` (JUST 0) FALSE
#ASSERT `s 82(9) there was a failure to remit` (JUST 1) TRUE
#ASSERT `s 82(9) there was a failure to remit` NOTHING TRUE
-- (a): on the day or up to 3 days late 3%; 4 or 5 days 5%; 6 or 7 days 7%; later, or never, 10%.
#ASSERT `s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` (JUST 0) EQUALS 0.03
#ASSERT `s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` (JUST 1) EQUALS 0.03
#ASSERT `s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` (JUST 3) EQUALS 0.03
#ASSERT `s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` (JUST 4) EQUALS 0.05
#ASSERT `s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` (JUST 5) EQUALS 0.05
#ASSERT `s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` (JUST 6) EQUALS 0.07
#ASSERT `s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` (JUST 7) EQUALS 0.07
#ASSERT `s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` (JUST 8) EQUALS 0.10
#ASSERT `s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` (JUST 30) EQUALS 0.10
#ASSERT `s 82(9)(a) the rate of the penalty by the lateness` NOTHING EQUALS 0.10
-- The rate, with the manner and with paragraph (b).
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 0) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 0) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.03
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST (0 MINUS 1)) FALSE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.03
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 3) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.03
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 4) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.05
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 5) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.05
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 6) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.07
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 7) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.07
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 8) TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.10
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` NOTHING TRUE FALSE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.10
-- (b): 20% needs BOTH an earlier penalty payable that year AND a knowing or grossly negligent failure; it prevails over (a).
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 1) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST 0.20
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` NOTHING TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST 0.20
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 1) TRUE TRUE FALSE EQUALS JUST 0.03
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 1) TRUE FALSE TRUE EQUALS JUST 0.03
-- (b) needs a failure: on time and in the required manner, no penalty even if both (b) facts are asserted.
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the rate of the penalty for failure to remit` (JUST 0) TRUE TRUE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
-- The amount of the penalty is the rate times the amount that was to be remitted.
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the penalty in dollars` 10_000 (JUST 0.03) EQUALS JUST 300
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the penalty in dollars` 1_000 (JUST 0.20) EQUALS JUST 200
#ASSERT `s 82(9) the penalty in dollars` 10_000 NOTHING EQUALS NOTHING

§ `s 82.01 excess payment deemed not deducted`

-- Arguments: year for which deducted; calendar year of the deduction; clerical/administrative/system error; election day;
-- the day of repayment or arrangement, if any; correcting return filed first; additional conditions met.
-- The deduction was in 2026, so the third year after is 2029 and it ends on 31 December 2029.
#ASSERT `s 82.01(1) the amount is deemed not to have been deducted` 2026 2026 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2029 12 31) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2029 12 31)) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT `s 82.01(1) the amount is deemed not to have been deducted` 2016 2016 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2019 12 31) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2019 6 1)) FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.01(1) the amount is deemed not to have been deducted` 2026 2026 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2029 12 31)) FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.01(1) the amount is deemed not to have been deducted` 2026 2026 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2029 12 31) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2030 1 1)) FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.01(1) the amount is deemed not to have been deducted` 2026 2026 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2029 12 31) NOTHING FALSE TRUE)
-- "For a year after 2015": 2015 itself is out, 2016 is in (above).
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.01(1) the amount is deemed not to have been deducted` 2015 2015 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2018 12 31) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2018 6 1)) FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.01(1) the amount is deemed not to have been deducted` 2026 2026 FALSE (YearMonthDay 2028 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2028 1 1)) FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.01(1) the amount is deemed not to have been deducted` 2026 2026 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2028 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2028 1 1)) TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.01(1) the amount is deemed not to have been deducted` 2026 2026 TRUE (YearMonthDay 2028 1 1) (JUST (YearMonthDay 2028 1 1)) FALSE FALSE)
-- (2): the amount deducted (500), or A minus B if that is less than it.
#ASSERT `s 82.01(2) the amount deemed not to have been deducted` 500 10_000 9_700 EQUALS 300
#ASSERT `s 82.01(2) the amount deemed not to have been deducted` 500 10_000 9_400 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `s 82.01(2) the amount deemed not to have been deducted` 500 10_000 9_500 EQUALS 500
#ASSERT `s 82.01(2) the amount deemed not to have been deducted` 500 10_000 9_999 EQUALS 1

§ `s 82.1 succession of employers`

-- Arguments: year; succeeds immediately; by formation/dissolution of a corporation; by an acquisition; with agreement; by operation of law.
#ASSERT `s 82.1 the successor employer may take into account the amounts deducted, remitted or paid by the former employer` 2004 TRUE TRUE FALSE FALSE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 82.1 the successor employer may take into account the amounts deducted, remitted or paid by the former employer` 2026 TRUE FALSE TRUE TRUE FALSE
#ASSERT `s 82.1 the successor employer may take into account the amounts deducted, remitted or paid by the former employer` 2026 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.1 the successor employer may take into account the amounts deducted, remitted or paid by the former employer` 2026 TRUE FALSE TRUE FALSE FALSE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.1 the successor employer may take into account the amounts deducted, remitted or paid by the former employer` 2003 TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.1 the successor employer may take into account the amounts deducted, remitted or paid by the former employer` 2026 FALSE TRUE TRUE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.1 the successor employer may take into account the amounts deducted, remitted or paid by the former employer` 2026 TRUE FALSE FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT `s 82.1 the successor employer shall also take them into account with respect to the employee's premium` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 82.1 the successor employer shall also take them into account with respect to the employee's premium` FALSE)

§ `s 83 liability of directors`

#ASSERT `s 83(1) the person is jointly and severally liable with the corporation` TRUE TRUE TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 83(1) the person is jointly and severally liable with the corporation` FALSE TRUE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 83(1) the person is jointly and severally liable with the corporation` TRUE FALSE TRUE)
#ASSERT NOT (`s 83(1) the person is jointly and severally liable with the corporation` TRUE TRUE FALSE)
-- The amount, with related interest and penalties: 1,000 + 50 + 30.
#ASSERT `s 83(1) the amount for which the directors are liable together with the corporation` 1_000 50 30 EQUALS 1_080
#ASSERT `s 83(2) subsections 227.1(2) to (7) of the Income Tax Act apply to the person` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 83(2) subsections 227.1(2) to (7) of the Income Tax Act apply to the person` FALSE)
#ASSERT `s 83(3) the assessment provisions of this Part apply to the person as if they were the employer` TRUE
#ASSERT NOT (`s 83(3) the assessment provisions of this Part apply to the person as if they were the employer` FALSE)

§ `s 84 the employer's premium is not recoverable`

#ASSERT `s 84 the employer is entitled to recover the amount from the person` TRUE TRUE EQUALS JUST FALSE
-- The section speaks of the employer's premium and the insured person only; nothing else is covered.
#ASSERT `s 84 the employer is entitled to recover the amount from the person` FALSE TRUE EQUALS NOTHING
#ASSERT `s 84 the employer is entitled to recover the amount from the person` TRUE FALSE EQUALS NOTHING
